### Public: list jobs
GET http://localhost:8080/api/jobs

### Public: list active jobs
GET http://localhost:8080/api/jobs?status=ACTIVE

### Public: get one job
GET http://localhost:8080/api/jobs/1

### Login first in a REST client and keep the JSESSIONID cookie for protected requests.
### ADMIN login example. Use your own seeded admin account.
POST http://localhost:8080/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email=admin@example.com&password=Admin123!

### ADMIN required: create job
POST http://localhost:8080/api/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "QA Analyst Co-op",
  "companyName": "Fictional Testing Ltd",
  "location": "Toronto",
  "category": "Technology",
  "employmentType": "CO_OP",
  "description": "Test web application features.",
  "requirements": "Attention to detail and basic SQL.",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### ADMIN required: update job
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/jobs/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated QA Analyst Co-op",
  "companyName": "Fictional Testing Ltd",
  "location": "Toronto",
  "category": "Technology",
  "employmentType": "CO_OP",
  "description": "Test web application features.",
  "requirements": "Attention to detail and basic SQL.",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### ADMIN required: delete job
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/jobs/1

### ADMIN required: list applications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications

### ADMIN can view any application; APPLICANT can only view their own application
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1

### ADMIN required: JDBC dashboard statistics
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/statistics

### ADMIN can view any user; APPLICANT can only request their own user id
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications/user/1

### ADMIN required: update application status
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "UNDER_REVIEW"
}
